Done. `pipeline_refactored.py` is on disk and verified. Here's the diff against the original:

### Changes

| Before | After |
|---|---|
| `DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE` etc. hardcoded at module level | `Config` dataclass loaded from `os.getenv(...)` — `LOG_FILE_PATH`, `METRICS_DB_PATH`, `DB_HOST`/`PORT`/`USER`/`PASS`, `REPORT_OUTPUT_PATH` |
| `c.execute("INSERT ... VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d)" % (...))` — SQL injection via `%` formatting | `conn.executemany("INSERT ... VALUES (?, ?, ?)", [...])` — parameterised queries |
| One 117-line `proc_data()` doing everything | `extract_logs()` → `aggregate_errors()` / `compute_api_latency()` / `track_active_sessions()` → `write_db()` / `write_report()` — clear ETL |
| `line.split(" ")`, string index arithmetic, manual loops to rebuild message | Regex `_LINE_RE`/`_USER_RE`/`_API_RE` with named capture groups |
| No type hints, no docstrings, bare `open()` | Type hints on every function, dataclasses for all record types, docstrings on public functions, `with open(...)` context managers, f-strings |
| Module-level dead Postgres constants (never used, SQLite only) | Kept as env-var config entries for future-proofing; actual connection uses the env-configurable `db_path` |
| Sample log seeding inline in `if __name__` | Moved to `_seed_sample_log()` helper |

